From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 14:55:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 246/638] ozone: dispatch native AROS input events [chromium]
 [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-4-ozone

AI_STATUS: implemented

ROOT_CAUSE: The AROS Ozone window subscribed only to lifecycle IDCMP classes and dispatched no Chromium input events. After adding native dispatch, mouse release events cleared persistent button state before construction and omitted the changed button from event.flags(), so release-triggered controls such as modal buttons never activated.

FIX_REASON: Translate AROS pointer motion, buttons, wheel raw keys, keyboard raw keys, modifiers, and repeats into Chromium ui::Events, and retain the changed button in release-event flags while clearing persistent pointer state.

SCOPE: ui/ozone/platform/aros/aros_window.cc and ui/ozone/platform/aros/aros_window.h only. Native Intuition framing remains unchanged; borderless Chromium-owned non-client UI is deferred.

VALIDATION: Bundled clang-format --dry-run --Werror and git diff --check pass; focused and in-tree AROS object builds pass; full Chrome link and ET_REL consolidation pass; hosted physical replay changes the local page to RESULT: accepted. Runtime SHA-256 f7d9e97d1e06482a7472b374bea164b06748a3a3bf42f410de665789861b74cf. Native runtime confirmation remains delegated.

RISK: Medium. This is the initial native AROS input backend; key mapping currently follows the standard US raw-key layout. Mouse release flags now follow Chromium event semantics.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap,
